     If an error occurs, ttccggeettppggrrpp() returns -1 and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o
     is set to indicate the error, as follows:

     [EBADF]            The _f_d argument is not a valid file descriptor.

     [ENOTTY]           The calling process does not have a controlling termi‐
                        nal or the underlying terminal device represented by
                        _f_d is not the controlling terminal.

